 Dear GlucoModicum hiring team,

I am Babak Firoozi Fooladi, applying for the data platform engineer role at GlucoModicum. I am drawn to this position because of its close collaboration with researchers and data professionals. Being in the prediabetic stage myself, a needle-free glucose monitor that transforms daily life for people with diabetes is a mission I would be proud to support—and a technology I may well rely on in the future.

My background (besides research) is in building reliable, reproducible data systems for research teams (who nicknamed me the team's "data wizard"). At Aalto University, I architected and manage our research data infrastructure: a partitioned data lake with DuckDB-based querying, automated Azure Functions pipelines in Python, and full technical documentation. Given the sensitive nature of our work, I also handle GDPR compliance, confidentiality, and data anonymisation. Most recently, as a consultant, I led a production codebase migration from Pandas to Polars, introducing unit tests and refactoring design patterns. This resulted in an 86% speedup on key calculations, a 60% overall performance boost, and clean data structures that the client's AI tools could readily build upon. In addition, I designed and implemeted data pipelines using DBT to process building data from Nordic countries and the Netherlands.

Beyond engineering, my PhD gave me solid footing in biostatistics, survival analysis, time-series modelling, and econometrics. I am used to work that must be accurate, reproducible, and defensible, and I know how to translate between domain researchers and data systems. While I have not worked directly in a regulated medical environment, I treat lineage tracking and audit-ready data as essential discipline rather than nice-to-haves. I have set up my own homelab, and I am in the middle of learning process of platform engineering, orchestration and kubernetes. I pick up tools quickly and am ready to get productive on Databricks and the rest of your stack.

I would welcome the chance to discuss how I can help build a governed, traceable data platform for GlucoModicum's clinical studies and V&V activities. Thank you for your time and consideration.

Kind regards,

